Installing GRUB to the Target Boot Device

1. Verify that pseudo-filesystems (/dev, /proc, /sys) and EFI variables are accessible inside the environment.

2. Create the target GRUB directory and EFI mount point:

`mkdir -p /boot/grub /boot/efi`

3. Install the GRUB bootloader structures to the EFI system partition:

`grub-install --target=x86_64-efi --efi-directory=/boot/efi --bootloader-id=KLFS`

4. Verify that GRUB boot binaries and EFI modules were created successfully:

`ls -lh /boot/grub/x86_64-efi`
`ls -lh /boot/efi/EFI/KLFS`
